From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:10:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] GPU path: line loops, quad strips and polygons; a control
 shader for patches without one; texture-to-buffer copies; primitive restart,
 rasterizer discard, depth clamp, line width; finalized textures stay
 samplable; coverage report; framediff

nvn_gpu: stand-in textures and ignored state are counted by reason and listed as cases; learn_type retranslates a shader with the texture type the game binds when the translator takes it from the table; texture-to-buffer copy reads the region back; copies between formats of the same texel size are raw copies.
nvn_spirv: passthrough_tcs makes the control shader the hardware has when a program has none. framediff.py compares frames with references.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux milestone D: every draw the GPU path skipped or made with a stand-in is counted by reason; the primitives, tessellation without a control shader, texture-to-buffer copies and draw state the game sets are done
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch Téo/jalon-d-graphique)

